Hi,

I haven't seen it before (though I am also not a big
RmaBackgroundCorrection user).  However, it could be the reason why
Ken added options 'addJitter' and 'jitterSd' to add "jitter noise".
In some cases his values were very small and discrete values which
made the estimators fail converting.  I'm not sure if that could
result in NaN or not.

If NaN:s should never occur according to the model, we could test for
it while fitting the model.  This way these errors/odd results are
caught immediately.  Feel free to add such an assertion test.

Cheers

/Henrik

